#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:4
msgid "Peierls不安定性"
msgstr "Peierls Instability"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:6
msgid ""
"1次元の\\ :ref:`半充填<half-filling>`\\ の鎖を例に、原子の変位によって\\ :ref:`バンドギャップ"
"<valence-conduction-band-gap>`\\ が開き、格子が自発的に "
"変形する仕組みを見る。二量化による電子エネルギーの低下をSSH模型のバンドから求め、弾性エネルギーとの釣り合いから、 "
"二量化の大きさとギャップを導く。最後に、原子核を固定した鎖に現れる結合次数波との違いを扱う。"
msgstr ""
"A one-dimensional \\ :ref:`half-filled <half-filling>` \\ chain "
"illustrates how atomic displacements open a \\ :ref:`band gap <valence-"
"conduction-band-gap>` \\ and cause the lattice to deform spontaneously. "
"We obtain the reduction in electronic energy due to dimerization from the"
" bands of the SSH model, then derive the magnitude of the dimerization "
"and the gap from the balance with elastic energy. Finally, we distinguish"
" dimerization from the bond-order wave that appears in a chain with fixed"
" nuclei."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:10
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`SSH模型<tb-ssh>`、:ref:`半充填<half-filling>`、:ref:`状態の和とBZ積分"
"<bz-average>`、:ref:`結合次数<bond_order>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: The :ref:`SSH model <tb-ssh>`, :ref:`half filling "
"<half-filling>`, :ref:`sums over states and Brillouin-zone integration "
"<bz-average>`, and :ref:`bond order <bond_order>`."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:12
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:14
msgid "格子の二量化でゾーン境界にギャップが開き、半充填の鎖の電子エネルギーが下がることを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain how lattice dimerization opens a gap at the zone boundary and "
"lowers the electronic energy of a half-filled chain."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:15
msgid ""
"二量化による電子エネルギーの低下が :math:`\\delta^2\\ln(1/\\delta)` "
"の形になることを示し、弾性エネルギーとの釣り合いから、 半充填の1次元鎖が弱い結合でも二量化することと、二量化の大きさを導く。"
msgstr ""
"Show that the electronic energy lowering due to dimerization has the form"
" :math:`\\delta^2\\ln(1/\\delta)`. Use the balance with elastic energy to"
" show that a half-filled one-dimensional chain dimerizes even at weak "
"coupling and to derive the magnitude of the dimerization."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:17
msgid "原子変位を伴うPeierls歪みと、原子を固定した鎖の結合次数波を区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Distinguish a Peierls distortion involving atomic displacements from a "
"bond-order wave in a chain with fixed atoms."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:20
msgid "格子の二量化とバンドギャップ"
msgstr "Lattice Dimerization and the Band Gap"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:22
msgid ""
"等間隔に並んだ原子の間隔が長短交互になる変形を考える。この変形を二量化と呼ぶ。 鎖の周期は2倍になり、隣接原子間のホッピングも交替する。\\ "
":ref:`SSH模型<tb-ssh>`\\ では、 この交替によって元の鎖のフェルミ波数にギャップが開く（式 :eq:`tb-ssh-"
"gap`）。 :numref:`fig-tightbinding-ssh-bulk-gap`\\ "
"の右では、二量化後のゾーン境界にギャップが開いている。 半充填では下側のバンドが占有され、占有状態のエネルギーが下がる。"
msgstr ""
"Consider deforming a chain of equally spaced atoms so that the spacings "
"alternate between short and long. This deformation is called "
"dimerization. The chain's period doubles, and hopping between neighboring"
" atoms alternates. In the \\ :ref:`SSH model <tb-ssh>`\\ , the "
"alternation opens a gap at the Fermi wave number of the original chain "
"(Equation :eq:`tb-ssh-gap`). In :numref:`fig-tightbinding-ssh-bulk-gap` "
"\\  (right panel), the gap is at the zone boundary after dimerization. At"
" half filling, the lower band is occupied and the occupied states are "
"lowered in energy."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:28
msgid ""
"格子を変形させるには弾性エネルギーが必要である。電子エネルギーの低下が弾性エネルギーの "
"増加を上回ると、全エネルギーが下がり、鎖は自発的に二量化する。これが1次元鎖の **Peierls不安定性** である "
"[Heeger1988]_。以下の2節で、二つのエネルギーを式で比べる。"
msgstr ""
"Deforming the lattice costs elastic energy. If the decrease in electronic"
" energy exceeds the increase in elastic energy, the total energy falls "
"and the chain dimerizes spontaneously. This is the **Peierls "
"instability** of a one-dimensional chain [Heeger1988]_. The next two "
"sections compare the expressions for the two energies."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:35
msgid "二量化による電子エネルギーの低下"
msgstr "Lowering of the Electronic Energy by Dimerization"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"二量化の大きさを、交替するホッピング :math:`t_{1,2}=t(1\\pm\\delta)`\\ "
"（:math:`\\delta>0`）の相対的な変化 :math:`\\delta` で表す。 SSH模型のバンド :eq:`tb-ssh-"
"band` "
"に代入すると、:math:`t_1^2+t_2^2=2t^2(1+\\delta^2)`、:math:`2t_1t_2=2t^2(1-\\delta^2)`"
" から、 :math:`\\varepsilon_0` を基準にした下側のバンドは"
msgstr ""
"Express the magnitude of dimerization using the relative change in the "
"alternating hoppings :math:`t_{1,2}=t(1\\pm\\delta)` \\ "
"(:math:`\\delta>0`), denoted by :math:`\\delta`. Substituting into the "
"band of the SSH model in Equation :eq:`tb-ssh-band` and using "
":math:`t_1^2+t_2^2=2t^2(1+\\delta^2)` and "
":math:`2t_1t_2=2t^2(1-\\delta^2)` gives the lower band relative to "
":math:`\\varepsilon_0`:"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:41
#, python-brace-format
msgid "E_-(k)=-2t\\sqrt{\\cos^2ka+\\delta^2\\sin^2ka}"
msgstr "E_-(k)=-2t\\sqrt{\\cos^2ka+\\delta^2\\sin^2ka}"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:46
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`\\delta=0` では一様な鎖のバンド :math:`-2t|\\cos ka|` を縮小ゾーンに折り返したものに戻り、"
" :math:`\\delta>0` ではゾーン境界 :math:`k=\\pm\\pi/(2a)` の付近の準位が下がる。"
msgstr ""
"At :math:`\\delta=0`, this reduces to the uniform-chain band "
":math:`-2t|\\cos ka|` folded into the reduced zone, whereas at "
":math:`\\delta>0`, the levels near the zone boundary "
":math:`k=\\pm\\pi/(2a)` move down in energy."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:49
msgid ""
"半充填では、縮小ゾーン :math:`-\\pi/(2a)<k\\le\\pi/(2a)` "
"の下側のバンドに、各波数でスピンを含めて2個の電子が入る。 原子 :math:`N` 個の鎖には単位胞が :math:`N/2` "
"個あるので、波数の和を\\ :ref:`積分に置き換える<bz-average>`\\ と （縮小ゾーンの幅は "
":math:`\\pi/a`）、1原子あたりの電子エネルギーは"
msgstr ""
"At half filling, the lower band in the reduced zone "
":math:`-\\pi/(2a)<k\\le\\pi/(2a)` contains two electrons per wave number,"
" counting spin. A chain of :math:`N` atoms has :math:`N/2` unit cells, so"
" \\ :ref:`replacing the sum over wave numbers with an integral <bz-"
"average>` \\ (the reduced zone has width :math:`\\pi/a`) gives the "
"electronic energy per atom:"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:53
msgid ""
"E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)=\\frac{a}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi/(2a)}^{\\pi/(2a)}E_-(k)\\,\\mathrm"
" dk\n"
"=-\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{\\cos^2x+\\delta^2\\sin^2x}\\,\\mathrm"
" dx"
msgstr ""
"E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)=\\frac{a}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi/(2a)}^{\\pi/(2a)}E_-(k)\\,\\mathrm"
" dk\n"
"=-\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi/2}^{\\pi/2}\\sqrt{\\cos^2x+\\delta^2\\sin^2x}\\,\\mathrm"
" dx"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:59
msgid ""
"である。:math:`\\delta=0` では :math:`E_{\\mathrm{el}}(0)=-4t/\\pi` "
"で、一様な鎖の半充填の値に一致する。積分は第2種完全楕円積分で、 :math:`\\delta` が小さいときに展開すると"
msgstr ""
"At :math:`\\delta=0`, :math:`E_{\\mathrm{el}}(0)=-4t/\\pi`, the half-"
"filled value for the uniform chain. The integral is a complete elliptic "
"integral of the second kind. Expanding for small :math:`\\delta` gives"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:62
msgid ""
"\\Delta "
"E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)=E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)-E_{\\mathrm{el}}(0)\n"
"\\simeq-\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,\\delta^2\\left(\\ln\\frac4\\delta-\\frac12\\right)"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta "
"E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)=E_{\\mathrm{el}}(\\delta)-E_{\\mathrm{el}}(0)\n"
"\\simeq-\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,\\delta^2\\left(\\ln\\frac4\\delta-\\frac12\\right)"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:68
msgid "を得る。数値積分と比べると、:math:`\\delta=0.1` で0.3%、:math:`\\delta=0.2` で約1%の差である。"
msgstr ""
"The expansion differs from numerical integration by 0.3% at "
":math:`\\delta=0.1` and about 1% at :math:`\\delta=0.2`."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:70
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"電子エネルギーは :math:`\\delta^2` に比例するだけでなく、:math:`\\ln(1/\\delta)` "
"が掛かって下がる。:math:`\\delta^2` の係数 :math:`-(2t/\\pi)\\ln(4/\\delta)` "
"は、:math:`\\delta\\to0` で負に発散する。ギャップが開くと、フェルミ準位の近くの状態は、 ギャップの大きさ "
":math:`4t\\delta` より離れたエネルギーのものまで少しずつ下がる。1次元の半充填の鎖では、フェルミ準位の 2点 "
":math:`\\pm k_{\\mathrm F}` "
"がちょうど新しいゾーン境界に重なるので、フェルミ準位の近くのすべての状態がこの低下に加わり、 その和が対数になる。"
msgstr ""
"The electronic energy lowering scales with :math:`\\delta^2` multiplied "
"by an additional factor of :math:`\\ln(1/\\delta)`. The coefficient of "
":math:`\\delta^2` is :math:`-(2t/\\pi)\\ln(4/\\delta)`, which diverges to"
" negative infinity as :math:`\\delta\\to0`. When the gap opens, states "
"near the Fermi level shift slightly down in energy, including states "
"farther away in energy than the gap size :math:`4t\\delta`. In a one-"
"dimensional half-filled chain, the two Fermi points :math:`\\pm "
"k_{\\mathrm F}` lie exactly at the new zone boundary, so every state near"
" the Fermi level contributes to the lowering. Their sum gives the "
"logarithm."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:79
msgid "弾性エネルギーとの釣り合い"
msgstr "Balance with Elastic Energy"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"隣り合う原子 :math:`n` と :math:`n+1` の間のホッピングが、間隔の変化に比例して "
":math:`t_{n,n+1}=t-\\alpha(u_{n+1}-u_n)`\\ （:math:`\\alpha>0`）と "
"変わるとする。:math:`u_n` は原子 :math:`n` の変位で、間隔が縮むほどホッピングが大きくなる。二量化 "
":math:`u_n=(-1)^nu` では、 結合の長さが :math:`\\mp2u` だけ交互に変わり、ホッピングは "
":math:`t\\pm2\\alpha u` になるので、:math:`\\delta=2\\alpha u/t` である。 "
"隣り合う原子をばね定数 :math:`K` のばねで結ぶと、1本の結合の弾性エネルギーは "
":math:`K(2u)^2/2`、結合は1原子あたり1本なので、"
msgstr ""
"Suppose hopping between neighboring atoms :math:`n` and :math:`n+1` "
"varies linearly with their change in spacing as "
":math:`t_{n,n+1}=t-\\alpha(u_{n+1}-u_n)` \\ (:math:`\\alpha>0`). Here "
":math:`u_n` is the displacement of atom :math:`n`, and hopping increases "
"as the spacing decreases. With dimerization :math:`u_n=(-1)^nu`, the bond"
" lengths alternate by :math:`\\mp2u`, and hopping becomes "
":math:`t\\pm2\\alpha u`, so :math:`\\delta=2\\alpha u/t`. If neighboring "
"atoms are connected by springs of spring constant :math:`K`, the elastic "
"energy per bond is :math:`K(2u)^2/2`. There is one bond per atom, so"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:86
msgid ""
"E_{\\mathrm{lat}}(\\delta)=2Ku^2=\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,g\\,\\delta^2,\\qquad"
" g=\\frac{\\pi Kt}{4\\alpha^2}"
msgstr ""
"E_{\\mathrm{lat}}(\\delta)=2Ku^2=\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,g\\,\\delta^2,\\qquad"
" g=\\frac{\\pi Kt}{4\\alpha^2}"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:91
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`g` は、ばねの硬さと電子と格子の結合の強さの比を表す無次元の数で、SSHらの結合定数 "
":math:`\\lambda=2\\alpha^2/(\\pi Kt)` とは :math:`g=1/(2\\lambda)` の関係にある "
"[Heeger1988]_。"
msgstr ""
"The dimensionless number :math:`g` describes the ratio of the spring "
"stiffness to the strength of the electron-lattice coupling. It is related"
" to the SSH coupling constant :math:`\\lambda=2\\alpha^2/(\\pi Kt)` by "
":math:`g=1/(2\\lambda)` [Heeger1988]_."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:94
msgid ":eq:`peierls-electronic-expansion` と足すと、1原子あたりのエネルギーの変化は"
msgstr ""
"Adding this to Equation :eq:`peierls-electronic-expansion` gives the "
"change in energy per atom:"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:96
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\Delta "
"E(\\delta)\\simeq\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,\\delta^2\\left(g+\\frac12-\\ln\\frac4\\delta\\right)"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta "
"E(\\delta)\\simeq\\frac{2t}{\\pi}\\,\\delta^2\\left(g+\\frac12-\\ln\\frac4\\delta\\right)"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:101
msgid ""
"である。:math:`\\ln(4/\\delta)` は :math:`\\delta\\to0` で限りなく大きくなるので、:math:`g`"
" がどれほど大きくても、十分小さい :math:`\\delta` では括弧の中が負になり、二量化でエネルギーが下がる。弾性エネルギーは "
":math:`\\delta^2` に比例するだけなので、 "
"電子エネルギーの対数の低下にいつかは負ける。これが、半充填の1次元鎖が絶対零度で必ず二量化するという "
"Peierls不安定性の中身である。:math:`\\mathrm d\\Delta E/\\mathrm d\\delta=0` から "
":math:`\\ln(4/\\delta_0)=g+1`、すなわち"
msgstr ""
"Since :math:`\\ln(4/\\delta)` grows without bound as "
":math:`\\delta\\to0`, however large :math:`g` is, at sufficiently small "
":math:`\\delta` the term in parentheses is negative and dimerization "
"lowers the energy. The elastic energy is only proportional to "
":math:`\\delta^2`, so the logarithmic lowering of electronic energy "
"eventually outweighs it. This is the Peierls instability: a half-filled "
"one-dimensional chain always dimerizes at absolute zero. The stationarity"
" condition :math:`\\mathrm d\\Delta E/\\mathrm d\\delta=0` gives "
":math:`\\ln(4/\\delta_0)=g+1`, or"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:106
msgid ""
"\\delta_0=4\\,e^{-1-g},\\qquad "
"\\Delta_{\\mathrm{SSH}}=2|t_1-t_2|=4t\\delta_0=16t\\,\\exp\\!\\left(-1-\\frac{\\pi"
" Kt}{4\\alpha^2}\\right)"
msgstr ""
"\\delta_0=4\\,e^{-1-g},\\qquad "
"\\Delta_{\\mathrm{SSH}}=2|t_1-t_2|=4t\\delta_0=16t\\,\\exp\\!\\left(-1-\\frac{\\pi"
" Kt}{4\\alpha^2}\\right)"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:111
msgid ""
"で極小になる（:numref:`fig-peierls-energy-"
"balance`）。:math:`\\Delta_{\\mathrm{SSH}}` は、この二量化で開くギャップ :eq:`tb-ssh-gap`"
" である。ばねが硬いほど、また結合 :math:`\\alpha` が弱いほど、二量化とギャップは "
"指数関数的に小さくなるが、0にはならない。:eq:`peierls-delta0` は :eq:`peierls-electronic-"
"expansion` の展開に基づくので、 :math:`\\delta_0` が小さい範囲の近似である。数値積分の :eq:`peierls-"
"electronic-energy` で極小を求めると、:math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.07`\\ "
"（:math:`g=3`）で1%、 :math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.2`\\ （:math:`g=2`）で約6%ずれる。"
msgstr ""
"at the minimum (:numref:`fig-peierls-energy-balance`). Here "
":math:`\\Delta_{\\mathrm{SSH}}` is the gap that opens with this "
"dimerization, as given by Equation :eq:`tb-ssh-gap`. Stiffer springs or "
"weaker coupling :math:`\\alpha` make the dimerization and the gap "
"exponentially small, but they remain nonzero. Equation :eq:`peierls-"
"delta0` uses the expansion in Equation :eq:`peierls-electronic-expansion`"
" and is therefore an approximation valid for small :math:`\\delta_0`. "
"Finding the minimum by numerical integration of Equation :eq:`peierls-"
"electronic-energy` gives a difference of 1% at "
":math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.07` \\ (:math:`g=3`) and about 6% at "
":math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.2` \\ (:math:`g=2`)."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:116
msgid "二量化の大きさに対するエネルギー。弾性エネルギーは放物線で増え、電子エネルギーの変化はそれより速く下がる。和は原点から少し下がって極小をとり、その後増える。"
msgstr ""
"Energy versus dimerization amplitude. The elastic energy increases "
"parabolically, and the change in electronic energy falls faster. The sum "
"falls slightly from the origin, reaches a minimum, and then rises."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:122
msgid ""
":math:`g=3` の弾性エネルギー :eq:`peierls-elastic-energy`\\ （赤の破線）、電子エネルギーの変化\\ "
"（青の破線、:eq:`peierls-electronic-energy` の数値積分）と、 その和（黒）。和は "
":math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.074` で極小になる。係数は説明用で、特定の物質の値ではない。"
msgstr ""
"For :math:`g=3`, the elastic energy in Equation :eq:`peierls-elastic-"
"energy` \\ is shown by a red dashed line, the change in electronic energy"
" \\ by a blue dashed line (numerical integration of Equation :eq"
":`peierls-electronic-energy`), and their sum by a black line. The sum "
"reaches a minimum at :math:`\\delta_0\\approx0.074`. The coefficients are"
" illustrative and do not represent a specific material."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:125
msgid ""
"2次元・3次元の結晶では、一般にフェルミ面の一部でしかギャップが開かないので、電子エネルギーの低下は対数で発散しない。 "
"その場合は、結合が十分強くなければ周期を変える変形はエネルギーを下げない。1次元の半充填の鎖で、どんなに弱い結合でも "
"不安定になるのは、フェルミ面（2点）全体がちょうど新しいゾーン境界に重なるためである。"
msgstr ""
"In two- and three-dimensional crystals, a gap generally opens over only "
"part of the Fermi surface, so the decrease in electronic energy does not "
"diverge logarithmically. In that case a deformation that changes the "
"period lowers the energy only if the coupling is sufficiently strong. A "
"half-filled one-dimensional chain becomes unstable even at arbitrarily "
"weak coupling because the entire Fermi surface (two points) lies exactly "
"at the new zone boundary."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:132
msgid "原子を固定した鎖の結合次数波"
msgstr "Bond-Order Waves in a Chain with Fixed Atoms"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:134
msgid ""
"原子核を等間隔に固定しても、電子状態の側で結合の強弱が交替することがある。 この状態を **結合次数波** （bond-order wave, "
"BOW）と呼ぶ。Peierls歪みには 原子変位が伴うので、計算結果を読むときは、結合次数の交替と原子間隔の交替を区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Even when nuclei are held at equal spacings, strong and weak bonds can "
"alternate in the electronic state. This state is called a **bond-order "
"wave** (BOW). A Peierls distortion involves atomic displacements, so "
"distinguish alternating bond orders from alternating atomic spacings when"
" interpreting calculation results."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:138
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-peierls-dimerization-and-bond-order`\\ で、原子の位置が動く二量化と、 "
"原子を固定したまま結合次数が交替する場合を見比べる。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-peierls-dimerization-and-bond-order` \\ compares "
"dimerization, in which the atoms move, with alternating bond orders while"
" the atoms stay fixed."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:141
msgid "上段は等間隔鎖。中段は原子間隔が短・長に交替する二量化。下段は原子位置を等間隔に保ったまま結合の強弱が交替する結合次数波。"
msgstr ""
"Top: equally spaced chain. Middle: dimerization with alternating short "
"and long atomic spacings. Bottom: bond-order wave with fixed atoms at "
"equal spacings and alternating strong and weak bonds."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:147
msgid "黒丸は原子位置、太い実線と細い破線は交替する結合の強・弱を示す。 縦の点線は、原子を固定した鎖での位置の目安である。"
msgstr ""
"Black circles mark atomic positions. Thick solid lines and thin dashed "
"lines show strong and weak bonds, respectively. The bond strengths "
"alternate. Vertical dotted lines mark the reference positions in the "
"chain with fixed atoms."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:150
msgid ""
"Hartree–Fock法などの平均場計算で結合次数波が現れる場合、\\ :ref:`結合次数<bond_order>`\\ を表す "
"隣接原子間の密度行列要素の交替が、交換項を通じて有効ハミルトニアンの隣接要素の交替を "
"生む。それがまた結合次数の交替を支えるという自己無撞着な関係になっている。 "
"SSH模型ではホッピングの交替を与えた上で、その結果として生じるギャップを記述する。"
msgstr ""
"When a bond-order wave appears in a mean-field calculation such as "
"Hartree–Fock, the density matrix elements between neighboring atoms, "
"which give the \\ :ref:`bond order <bond_order>`\\ , alternate. Through "
"the exchange term, this causes alternation in the corresponding nearest-"
"neighbor elements of the effective Hamiltonian, which in turn sustains "
"the alternating bond orders self-consistently. The SSH model prescribes "
"alternating hoppings and describes the resulting gap."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:158
msgid "説明用の事例：等間隔に固定した水素原子鎖の結合次数"
msgstr "Worked Example: Bond Orders in a Fixed, Equally Spaced Hydrogen Atom Chain"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:160
msgid ""
"「\\ :ref:`bond_order`\\ 」の説明用の事例では、計算事例 `水素原子を並べると電子バンドは生まれるのか "
"<https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/hydrogen_chain/band_formation.html>`_ の、原子間隔1.8 "
"Åで等間隔に並べた水素原子鎖（STO-3G、Psi4 1.10）について、隣り合う結合の結合次数を比べている。 "
"RHFでは、鎖の中央の結合次数が約0.86と0.38で交替し、交替の大きさは原子数を16、32、64と増やしてもほとんど変わらない。 RKS-"
"PBEの交替は小さく、原子数とともに小さくなり、端の効果として説明できる。スピン非制限計算では、交替はほぼ消える。"
msgstr ""
"The worked example in \\ :ref:`Bond Order <bond_order>` \\ compares bond "
"orders of adjacent bonds in a hydrogen atom chain with a uniform spacing "
"of 1.8 Å (STO-3G, Psi4 1.10) from the calculation example `Does a Chain "
"of Hydrogen Atoms Form an Electronic Band? <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/hydrogen_chain/band_formation.html>`_. With RHF, bond"
" orders near the center alternate between about 0.86 and 0.38, with "
"little change in the amplitude of the alternation as the atom count "
"increases from 16 to 32 to 64. With RKS-PBE the alternation is small, "
"decreases as the number of atoms grows, and can be explained as an end "
"effect. In spin-unrestricted calculations the alternation almost "
"disappears."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:166
msgid ""
"原子は等間隔に固定してあるので、RHFで見える交替はPeierls歪みではなく、電子状態の側の結合次数波である。 "
"しかも、交替が現れるかどうかは、計算手法（電子間相互作用の扱い）によって変わる。原子が実際に二量化するかを知るには、 "
"原子位置も最適化して、原子間隔が交替するか、そのときエネルギーが下がるかを調べる必要がある。"
msgstr ""
"The atoms are held at equal spacings, so the alternation seen in RHF is "
"an electronic bond-order wave rather than a Peierls distortion. Moreover,"
" whether the alternation appears depends on the calculation method (the "
"treatment of electron–electron interactions). To find out whether the "
"atoms actually dimerize, also optimize their positions and check whether "
"the spacings alternate and whether this lowers the energy."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:173
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:175
msgid ""
"本稿の模型は、原子を静止させたまま電子状態を求め、そのエネルギーを弾性エネルギーと比べる。原子核の零点振動や、 "
"電子どうしの相互作用は含まない。電子間相互作用が強い鎖では、結合次数波や、スピンが交互に並ぶ状態が、 "
"二量化と競合する（上の事例でも、手法によって結果が変わる）。"
msgstr ""
"In this model, the electronic state is calculated with the atoms held "
"stationary and its energy is compared with the elastic energy. Nuclear "
"zero-point motion and electron–electron interactions are omitted. In "
"chains with strong electron–electron interactions, bond-order waves and "
"states with alternating spins compete with dimerization, as illustrated "
"by the dependence on method in the example above."

#: ../../solid/peierls_instability.rst:179
msgid ""
"絶対零度を考えた。有限温度では、ギャップをまたぐ熱励起が電子エネルギーの利得を減らすので、ある温度より上では "
"二量化しない（Peierls転移）。厳密な1次元の系では揺らぎが長距離の秩序を壊すので、実際に二量化が観測されるのは、 "
"鎖どうしが弱く結びついた擬1次元の物質である。ポリアセチレンの単結合と二重結合の交替は、SSH模型で説明される代表例である "
"[Heeger1988]_。"
msgstr ""
"We considered absolute zero. At finite temperature, thermal excitation "
"across the gap reduces the electronic energy gain, so dimerization "
"disappears above a certain temperature (the Peierls transition). In "
"strictly one-dimensional systems, fluctuations destroy long-range order, "
"so dimerization is actually observed in quasi-one-dimensional materials, "
"in which the chains are weakly coupled. The alternating single and double"
" bonds of polyacetylene are a classic example explained by the SSH model "
"[Heeger1988]_."

